-- 0025: restructure the hadith library down to five collections.
--
-- The app now offers exactly five books, in this order:
--   0 nawawi40       الأربعون النووية      (seeded in 0015 — untouched here)
--   1 qudsi40        الأربعون القدسية      (seeded in 0015 — untouched here)
--   2 arbaeen_imaniyya  الأربعين الإيمانية (collection row only — SEE BELOW)
--   3 bulugh_almaram    بلوغ المرام
--   4 umdat_alahkam     العمدة في الأحكام
--
-- The six Kutub al-Sittah seeded in 0016-0021 (~34k hadith) are NOT dropped:
-- importing them was substantial work and the client may want them back. They
-- are only unpublished. content.hadith_collections rows keep every entry; the
-- content API (functions/api/supabase_content_repo.ts) filters both the list
-- and the detail endpoint on `hadith_collections.published = true`, so an
-- unpublished collection is invisible to /v1/content/hadith-collections and to
-- /v1/content/hadith-collections/<slug>, while all rows stay queryable in the
-- database and via the admin API. Re-enable with:
--   update content.hadith_collections set published = true, updated_at = now()
--    where slug in ('bukhari','muslim','abudawud','tirmidhi','nasai','ibnmajah');
--
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- SOURCING (religious text — nothing here was written, paraphrased or
-- reconstructed by hand; every entry is the verbatim Arabic matn of a real
-- published edition, with the editor's apparatus stripped and nothing added).
--
-- بلوغ المرام / bulugh_almaram — 1564 entries
--   Source:    المكتبة الشاملة, book #17757 — «بلوغ المرام من أدلة الأحكام»,
--              ابن حجر العسقلاني (ت ٨٥٢ هـ), tahqiq د. ماهر ياسين الفحل,
--              دار القبس، الرياض، ط١ ١٤٣٥هـ/٢٠١٤م.
--              https://shamela.ws/book/17757
--              retrieved as machine-readable JSON from the Shamela mirror
--              https://files.turath.io/books-v3/17757.json on 2026-07-31.
--   Extraction: per text block, everything after the `_________` rule (the
--              muhaqqiq's takhrij footnotes) was dropped, `<span data-type=
--              'title'>` chapter headings and `⦗page⦘` markers removed,
--              `(n)` footnote markers removed, whitespace normalised. Entries
--              are keyed on the edition's printed hadith number. Numbers 333
--              and 1449 do not exist in this edition's numbering; 189/190 and
--              677/678 are each one text carrying two numbers, stored under the
--              first of the pair — hence 1564 rows over a 1..1568 range.
--   Cross-check: 185/185 sampled entries have a 6-word run present in the
--              independent sunnah.com-derived corpus (AhmedBaset/hadith-json,
--              db/by_book/other_books/bulugh_almaram.json). Confidence: high.
--
-- العمدة في الأحكام / umdat_alahkam — 414 entries
--   Source:    المكتبة الشاملة, book #538 — «العمدة في الأحكام»,
--              عبد الغني المقدسي (ت ٦٠٠ هـ), tahqiq عبد المحسن بن محمد القاسم
--              (متون طالب العلم), ط٢ ١٤٤٢هـ/٢٠٢١م.
--              https://shamela.ws/book/538
--              retrieved from https://files.turath.io/books-v3/538.json on
--              2026-07-31. Same extraction rules as above.
--              Numbering is complete and contiguous: 1..414, no gaps.
--   Cross-check: 408/409 entries have a 6-word run present in an independent
--              digitisation of a different edition (Shamela #6075,
--              ت. محمود الأرناؤوط). The single outlier (#146, حديث الكسوف
--              عن أبي موسى) is an edition difference, not a transcription
--              error. Confidence: high.
--
-- الأربعين الإيمانية / arbaeen_imaniyya — 0 entries. NOT SOURCED.
--   No work under this title could be located in any reputable
--   machine-readable corpus: it is absent from fawazahmed0/hadith-api,
--   AhmedBaset/hadith-json (17 books incl. three forties), المكتبة الشاملة /
--   turath.io, and sunnah.com, and no authoritative bibliographic record of a
--   book by this exact name was found. Rather than invent, paraphrase or
--   reconstruct scripture, the collection row is seeded EMPTY. Someone must
--   identify the intended work (author + edition) and supply its text before
--   this book has any content.
--
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- REVIEW GATE (migration 0014). Every entry imported here lands with
-- review_status = 'pending' and published = false — the check constraint
-- `not published or review_status = 'approved'` is satisfied, and nothing
-- unreviewed can reach the API. The collection rows are published so the app
-- offers the five books, but their entries stay dark until a scholar signs off.
-- 0014's content.needs_review view lists exactly these rows. To release a
-- book after review:
--   update content.hadith_entries e set review_status = 'approved',
--          reviewed_by = '<reviewer>', reviewed_at = now(), published = true,
--          updated_at = now()
--     from content.hadith_collections c
--    where c.id = e.collection_id and c.slug = 'bulugh_almaram';

-- 1. Hide the Kutub al-Sittah without losing a single row. ------------------
update content.hadith_collections set published = false, updated_at = now()
 where slug in ('bukhari', 'muslim', 'abudawud', 'tirmidhi', 'nasai', 'ibnmajah')
   and published;

-- 2. الأربعين الإيمانية — collection row only, deliberately with no entries.
on conflict (app_id, slug) do update set
  name_translations = excluded.name_translations,
  description_translations = excluded.description_translations,
  sort_order = excluded.sort_order,
  published = excluded.published,
  updated_at = now();

-- 3. بلوغ المرام. -----------------------------------------------------------
-- Dollar-quote tag $fb$ (not $$): some matn contains a literal "$$" that would
-- otherwise close the block early.
do $fb$
declare col_id uuid;
begin
  on conflict (app_id, slug) do update set
    name_translations = excluded.name_translations,
    description_translations = excluded.description_translations,
    sort_order = excluded.sort_order,
    published = excluded.published,
    updated_at = now()
  returning id into col_id;

